  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 120 AM CDT Mon Jun 1 2026\n\nDry conditions will persist at least to begin the week before rain \nchances return. Expect warmer conditions through this week with \nhighs in the 80s and 90s across the region with heat indices around \n100-105. This will lead to minor to moderate heat stress conditions. \n \nThe chances for showers and storms will return to the region this\nweek as the ridge weakens allowing for some shortwave energy to \ncreep into the region which will combine with the seabreeze each \nday. This will be coupled with a surge of moisture. The moisture \nwill be coming from a couple sources. One a mid-level low \ndeveloping off the southern California coast will funnel moisture \ninto the area as well as the presence of onshore flow from the \nGulf. These factors will allow for showers and thunderstorm \nactivity to increase beginning Tuesday through the remainder of \nthe week into the weekend. As the low nears the region it will \nincrease the coverage and chances across the region with the \nhighest chances being later in the week into the weekend. This \nwill be when the low is expected to push across the region to the \nnorth while sending some embedded shortwave energy into the \nregion. This will also be when the highest surges of moisture will\nbe expected. Will need to monitor the trends in PoP chances/cloud\ncover which could lead to slightly lower highs due to increasing \nmoisture.",
